menu "ROBOT-COMM-SECURE Configuration"

    config ROBOT_MASTER_KEY
        string "Master HMAC Key for Robot Registry"
        default "CHANGE_THIS_DEFAULT_KEY_12345"
        help
            This is the master HMAC-SHA256 key used to sign and verify robot 
            identity packets. It MUST be changed from the default value.
            
            IMPORTANT: In a production system, this key should be stored 
            securely (e.g., in an encrypted NVS partition or eFuse). 
            This config is for development and testing.

    config ROBOT_KEY_STORAGE_TYPE
        int "Key Storage Type"
        range 0 2
        default 0
        help
            Select how the master key is stored:
            0 - In application config (Kconfig) - FOR TESTING ONLY
            1 - In encrypted NVS partition
            2 - In eFuse (HMAC_UP peripheral)
            
            Using eFuse (option 2) provides the highest security as the 
            key is never exposed in flash or memory.

endmenu